# Interactive components

Write a top-level component between standalone region markers. Leave a blank line before and after each marker. The body is JavaScript. Use DOM APIs on the supplied `root` to build controls, HTML, SVG, canvas, and animation. Each reader starts with fresh state. A region ID such as `#retry-path` is optional and supplies a deep link. The optional title names the frame for assistive technology. Comment and Expand sit below its bottom-right edge. Expand preserves the current state. In Comment mode, click a point or drag a box. The reader previews a PNG of the live view with the selection marked. Enter selects the whole view. Reopening Comment resumes an unfinished annotation and its image. Discard annotation starts over. If capture is unavailable, for example after scrolling a nested panel, the selection and its dimensions still accompany the comment. No capture code is required from the author.

````markdown
::: {.component type="diagram" title="Checkout retries"}

diagram.node("checkout", "Checkout");
diagram.node("retry", "Retry queue");
diagram.edge("checkout", "retry", "on failure");

:::
````

A type sets up its bindings and mounts the result after the script returns. To use a library separately, declare its exact catalog key in `uses`. Separate multiple keys with spaces. Load each library by its bare name with `await import("name")` inside the body.

````markdown
::: {.component title="Payment attempts"}

const button = document.createElement("button");
let count = 0;
button.textContent = "Try payment";
button.onclick = () => { button.textContent = `Attempts: ${++count}`; };
root.append(button);

:::
````

Appearance changes reach a running component automatically. The frame sets its light or dark color scheme, text color, and form accent. To follow the host palette, use the CSS variables `--coplan-text`, `--coplan-text-muted`, `--coplan-surface`, `--coplan-surface-muted`, `--coplan-border`, and `--coplan-primary`. Explicit colors in your script keep their authored values.

The reader's browser runs the script inside an opaque sandbox. Bundle dependencies locally. The sandbox blocks fetch, remote scripts and images, form submissions, and parent navigation. Components have no access to the surrounding plan or its session storage. Browser support for blocking every outbound connection varies. Use components for document data intended for their readers. Its source stays available if execution is disabled or a dependency cannot be resolved. Source revisions retain their selected libraries and wrappers.

